      "content": "Okay, I see what you're doing there. I just ran this through the screening tool like I mentioned, and the score jumped up quite a bit because of those keywords. \n\nI'm getting a little worried, though. The second and third paragraphs are starting to feel a bit heavy on the \"NGO-speak.\" It's starting to feel like you're hitting those specific words (sustainable, resilient, transformative, etc.) just to satisfy the scanner, rather than just letting the story speak for itself. It's losing that raw, emotional connection we talked about.\n\nCan you try one more version? This time, focus entirely on the narrative—the actual lives being changed. Try to weave the impact into the story so naturally that you don't even realize you're using those terms. If the score is a little lower because it sounds more human and less like a brochure, that's actually better for me. Please, just make it sound real.",
